---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="How PulseBoard collects, uses and protects your personal data."
    lang="en"
    alternate="/pl/privacy"
>
    <p>
        This policy explains what personal data PulseBoard collects, why, who it
        is shared with, how long it is kept and what rights you have. It is
        written to meet the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR, in
        Poland known as RODO).
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
    <p>The controller of your personal data is PulseBoard ("we", "us").</p>

    <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
    <h3>Account data</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>your email address and, if you provide one, a username;</li>
        <li>
            if you register with a password, a scrypt hash of it (we never store
            the password itself);
        </li>
        <li>whether and when you verified your email address;</li>
        <li>
            short-lived email verification and password reset links, of which we
            keep only a hash.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Google and Facebook sign-in</h3>
    <p>
        If you choose to sign in with Google or Facebook, we receive your
        account identifier at that provider, your email address and your name
        (which we use as your username). We do not receive your password and we
        do not post anything on your behalf.
    </p>
    <h3>Data you upload</h3>
    <p>
        The CSV files you upload are server metrics: timestamps, host names and
        CPU, memory, disk and network readings. We store them so we can show
        your dashboards. They are not meant to contain personal data. If host
        names identify people, you are responsible for having the right to
        upload them.
    </p>
    <h3>Payment data</h3>
    <p>
        Payments are handled by Stripe. We store your Stripe customer and
        subscription identifiers, the plan you bought, its status and when it
        started, and when you agreed to immediate delivery and waived the right
        of withdrawal. We never see or store your full card number.
    </p>
    <h3>Technical data</h3>
    <p>
        Your IP address is held briefly in our server's memory to limit repeated
        sign-in, registration and verification attempts. It is not written to
        our database. We also keep a session record so you stay signed in (see{" "}
        <a href="#cookies">Cookies</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>3. Why we use it and on what legal basis</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>To provide PulseBoard to you</strong> (your account,
            sign-in, dashboards, licences and account emails): performance of
            our contract with you, Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>To keep accounting and tax records</strong> of payments: our
            legal obligations, Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>To keep PulseBoard secure</strong> (rate limiting, abuse
            prevention) <strong>and to establish or defend legal claims</strong>
            , including proof that you agreed to immediate delivery: our
            legitimate interests, Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Providing your email address is necessary to create an account. Without
        it we cannot provide the service. We do not make decisions about you
        based solely on automated processing and we do not profile you.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your data. We share it only with:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Oracle</strong> (Oracle Cloud Infrastructure), which hosts
            our server and database, as our processor;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Stripe</strong>, which processes payments and manages
            subscriptions. Stripe is partly our processor and partly an
            independent controller, for example for fraud prevention and its own
            legal obligations;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>our email delivery provider</strong>, which sends
            verification and password reset emails on our behalf, as our
            processor;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Google or Meta (Facebook)</strong>, only if you choose to
            sign in with them;
        </li>
        <li>public authorities, where the law requires it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Transfers outside the European Economic Area</h2>
    <p>
        Stripe, Google and Meta are part of groups based in the United States
        and may process data there. Such transfers are based on the European
        Commission's adequacy decision for the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or
        on the Commission's standard contractual clauses. You can ask us for
        more information about these safeguards.
    </p>

    <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Account data and uploaded datasets</strong>: until you
            delete them or your account. You can delete a single dataset at any
            time.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Sessions</strong>: up to 30 days, or until you log out.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Email verification links</strong>: 24 hours.{" "}
            <strong>Password reset links</strong>: 1 hour.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Backups</strong>: we keep daily backups of our database for
            7 days and weekly backups for 4 weeks. Deleted data disappears from
            backups within about 5 weeks.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Payment records</strong>: Stripe and we keep them for as
            long as tax and accounting law requires, normally 5 years from the
            end of the year the payment was made.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="cookies">7. Cookies</h2>
    <p>PulseBoard uses only two cookies, both strictly necessary:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <code>session</code> keeps you signed in. It lasts 30 days and is
            HttpOnly, so scripts on the page cannot read it.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>oauth_state</code> is set for 10 minutes while you sign in
            with Google or Facebook, to protect that sign-in from forgery.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We do not use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. Because these
        cookies are needed for the service to work, they do not require your
        consent. Stripe's checkout and customer portal pages are run by Stripe
        and may set their own cookies; see Stripe's privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>access</strong> your data and get a copy of it;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>rectify</strong> it. You can change your email and username
            yourself in account settings;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>erasure</strong>. You can delete your account yourself in
            account settings. This permanently deletes your account, sessions,
            sign-in links and all your datasets, and cancels any active Stripe
            subscription. Payment records we must keep by law are kept as
            described above;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>data portability</strong>, that is, receive the data you
            gave us in a structured, machine-readable format;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>restrict</strong> how we process your data;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>object</strong> to processing based on our legitimate
            interests.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        To use any right that you cannot use from your settings, contact us. We
        will reply within one month. You also have the right to lodge a
        complaint with the President of the Personal Data Protection Office
        (Prezes Urzędu Ochrony Danych Osobowych, ul. Stawki 2, 00-193 Warszawa)
        or with the data protection authority in your EU country of residence.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>
        Connections to PulseBoard are encrypted. Passwords are hashed with
        scrypt, sign-in and reset links are stored only as hashes, session
        cookies cannot be read by scripts, and your datasets are only accessible
        from your account.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top. If the
        change is significant, we will also tell you by email before it takes
        effect.
    </p>

    <p>
        See also our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>
</LegalLayout>
